{
  "about": "OH's regional seed (Lane D1, 2026-10-02), the kit's region section (scripts/demo-kit/lib/region.mjs, validated by lib/config.mjs) over the five dimensions the regional allowlist names (design §3: category, type, sizeBand, priceTier, fuel), with the exact values of public/oh/products.json. Synthetic and representative: not a claim about any state's market and never LG's sales; labelled synthetic → warehouse wherever it shows, until LG's regional rows replace it. Every state and DC is seeded: Texas and New Jersey verbatim (rehearsal regions A and B), the other 49 from the kit's income-tilt model, which blends only the TV rows (category tvs, keyed by type, size band and price tier) between the two; the appliance rows are the same national mix in every modelled state (extras), except cooking fuel: gas cooking about 38% nationally and about 70% in California and New Jersey (lg-buying-journeys.md §2, EIA RECS via NPGA), dryers 80% electric everywhere. The census shapes only this stand-in, never a score; price never varies by place or by person. The cold-start route's own vocabulary (the OH config's SEED_VOCABULARY) must equal `vocabulary` here.",
